+    "gate_that_fired": "acceptance_gate_wall_cap_did_not_bind_one_arm_only = False",
+    "sensitivity_excluding_wall_truncated_cells": {
+      "PRE_REGISTERED_CONSEQUENCE_HONORED": "acceptance_gates_note pre-registered that a False on this gate 'means the primary comparison is confounded and must be re-run with a larger cap'. The gate IS False. The pre-registered consequence is therefore APPLIED, not reinterpreted: the primary comparison is labelled CONFOUNDED pending a re-run at a larger cap. Overriding a pre-registered gate after seeing the data -- which is what calling it merely 'insensitive' amounted to -- is the failure this project's own discipline exists to prevent.",
+      "banked_31b": 3,
+      "banked_9b": 2,
+      "losses_31b": 0,
+      "ls20_is_a_MISSING_OBSERVATION_not_a_tie": "An earlier draft called ls20 'a 0-0 tie' and concluded the result was therefore 'insensitive' to the confound. That reasoning was circular: the 31B was cut off at 26 of 400 actions (6.5% of the budget) against the 9B's 391, so its 0 is a value never observed, not an observed tie. Recoded here as MISSING, which is why the action-matched 4-pair tally is the headline and the 5-pair version the inclusive variant.",
+      "n_pairs": 4,
+      "note": "Dropping the truncated cell changes neither the win/loss counts nor the direction. That bounds the damage to the DIRECTION -- it does not clear the gate.",
+      "primary_comparison_status": "CONFOUNDED_pending_rerun_at_larger_cap",
+      "win_loss_direction_changes": false,
+      "wins_31b": 1
+    },
+    "what_happened": [
+      "ls20: 31B hit the 900s soft wall cap (wall 1067s, timed_out=True) while the 9B did not (wall 228s). The 31B's result on this game (0 banked) is therefore CUT OFF, not converged."
+    ],
+    "why_it_is_reported_rather_than_suppressed": "The design forbids wall-clock from determining an ACTION-budgeted metric. This gate exists to catch exactly that and it fired correctly, so it is left FAILING. A gate quietly relaxed to make a run look clean is worse than the confound it hides."
+  },
+  "WHY_THE_PRIMARY_METRIC_MAY_BE_INSENSITIVE_TO_THE_INDUCER": {
+    "consequence": "Banked levels is the RIGHT metric for the submission decision (it is what scores), but it is a PARTIALLY INDUCER-INDEPENDENT metric: an arm can tie on banked levels while being strictly better at the thing the generator actually controls. That is precisely the pattern here -- tie-ish on banked levels, 0.4 vs 0.0 on plan_found. It means a null on banked levels does NOT license the conclusion that the generator is irrelevant; it licenses the narrower conclusion that, at this budget and support, the generator upgrade has not converted into score.",
+    "implication_for_design": "A future run wanting to isolate the inducer should either raise the action budget (so more levels require a plan rather than luck) or report banked levels SPLIT by whether a plan was installed before the level-up.",
+    "observation": "The 9B banked 2 levels (vc33) while its plan_found_rate was 0.0 on EVERY analyzed game -- i.e. those levels were reached by EXPLORATION, with no plan derived from any induced world model. So at a 400-action budget a substantial share of banked levels is produced by the explorer, not the inducer."
+  },
+  "acceptance_gate_both_arms_on_the_cuda_build_not_the_igpu": true,
