+  "acceptance_gates_note": "acceptance_gate_wall_cap_did_not_bind_one_arm_only is the fairness check that matters most for a SLOWER treatment arm: if the 900s tractability cap fired on the 31B and not the 9B, the 31B would have been handicapped on WALL-CLOCK, which the design explicitly forbids as a determinant of the ACTION-budgeted primary metric. A False here means the primary comparison is confounded and must be re-run with a larger cap. THIS GATE IS FALSE AND ITS PRE-REGISTERED CONSEQUENCE IS APPLIED: the primary comparison carries status CONFOUNDED_pending_rerun_at_larger_cap (see WALL_CAP_CONFOUND_AND_SENSITIVITY.primary_comparison_status). The direction is separately shown to be insensitive to the confound, but that bounds the damage -- it does NOT clear the gate, and an earlier draft that concluded 'insensitive' in place of the pre-registered consequence was overriding a gate after seeing the data.",
+  "answer_is_a_scored_submission_justified": {
+    "answer": "NO -- not on this evidence.",
+    "honest_reading": "Consistent with project_arc_actions_to_progress_metric: the binding constraint on the live path is dynamics induction quality reaching a USABLE plan, and while the 31B improves the plan-found rate, banked levels did not follow at this support. The migration remains justified on loadability and induction quality; it is NOT yet justified as a score improvement, and this measurement does not authorize a run. Note the primary metric is only PARTIALLY inducer-sensitive: the 9B banked 2 levels with plan_found_rate 0.0 everywhere, i.e. by exploration, so a banked-levels parity does NOT license the broader claim that the generator is irrelevant -- only the narrower one that it has not converted into score at this budget and support.",
+    "standing_gate": "feedback_arc3_online_gated_on_offline_beating_baselines: play the scored game only when an offline result beats BOTH a TRM baseline AND our best prior submitted Carnot run.",
+    "what_DID_move": "The 31B's upstream induction edge is visible downstream but stops short of score: plan_found_rate 0.4 vs 0.0 and engine_accepted_rate 0.4 vs 0.2. So the migration is NOT inert -- more of its induced world models survive the held-out verifier and yield a reachable plan. That is a real mechanism gain that has NOT yet converted into banked levels. Counterweight, stated rather than buried: hv_progress is the one paired secondary whose direction runs AGAINST the 31B (0 wins / 1 loss, mean delta -0.0233).",
+    "what_would_settle_it": "Raise the per-cell hard timeout to ~2400s so the 31B stops dropping its own hardest games (removing the selection effect), then run the full 12 games x >=2 seeds. Six discordant games are needed before p<0.05 is even reachable.",
+    "why_not": [
+      "The primary metric does not clear the gate: 1 discordant pair(s) out of n=5, two-sided p=1.0, and the MINIMUM reachable p at this discordance is 1.0. No direction is claimable at this support; the raw 3-vs-2 total rests on a single game.",
+      "The raw 3-vs-2 is an artifact of the pairing restriction. Over every cell each arm COMPLETED the tally is 31B 3 / 9B 3, and scoring a non-finisher as zero gives wins 1 / losses 1. Both bracketing tallies land on PARITY, because tu93 -- where the 9B banked a reproduction-gated level -- is one of the three games the 31B could not finish. The exclusion removes one 9B level and zero 31B levels.",
+      "Effective discriminating support is 2 of 5 pairs, not 5: on ft09, tr87 and ls20 NEITHER arm produced a usable plan, so those pairs are the same control agent twice and their ties carry no information about the inducer.",
+      "The wall-cap fairness gate is FALSE and its pre-registered consequence applies: the primary comparison is CONFOUNDED pending a re-run at a larger cap.",
+      "The analyzed subset is selection-biased toward games the 31B could finish (see SELECTION_EFFECT_ON_THE_PRIMARY_COMPARISON), and on the PRIMARY metric that bias runs IN THE 31B's FAVOR, not against it.",
