+  "duration_s_provenance": "Sum of per-cell wall_s across BOTH arms. Arms ran CONCURRENTLY on separate cards, so this exceeds the wall-clock span of the session; it is compute time, not elapsed time. Real GGUF load + real autoregressive generation on CUDA, measured 32.6 tok/s decode on the 31B.",
+  "experiment": "outer_loop_arc_heldout_31b_vs_9b_banked_levels",
+  "fairness_controls": {
+    "arm_prompt_configs": "Each model ran in ITS OWN live pin: 31B on arm 'frozen_gemma_pin' (no /no_think prefix -- gemma-4 has no such control token and would consume it as literal text), 9B on arm 'frozen' (/no_think, its shipped Qwen3 setting). Identical on every other knob (codeonly fence ON, 4096 n_predict, 3 tries). Forcing the retired Qwen prefix onto gemma would have reintroduced the thinking-budget confound.",
+    "both_arms_mtp_off": "The 9B's SHIPPED config is mtp=True, but _resolve_mtp_head() now resolves to the gemma-4-31B draft head staged for Kaggle, and pairing that head with the Qwen target kills the server outright ('Gemma4Assistant requires ctx_other to be set' -> '[spec] failed to measure draft model memory' -> exit). MTP is a decode-SPEED lever only, so under an ACTION budget it cannot move banked levels. Running BOTH arms MTP-off is symmetric and removes the mis-paired-head landmine. Kaggle's 31B arm would be ~1.4x faster in WALL-CLOCK only.",
+    "deviation_from_the_shipped_live_config": "n_ctx 32768 (shipped: 81920) and ffn_cpu_layers 0 (auto-fit would pick 7), for BOTH arms. FORCED, not preferred: at 81920 the VRAM guard needs 25388 MiB on a 24576 MiB card and even after auto-fit needs 24020 MiB against ~24123 free -- a ~100 MiB margin that any stray CUDA context loses, at which point _generator_server_and_env() falls through to the iGPU HIP build and the agent runs LLM-OFF while still reporting itself as the LLM-on path. That exact silent fallback happened in the design phase and was caught and discarded. The pool only has to satisfy K_concurrent*(prompt+max_tokens); this harness is single-threaded (K=1 -> 19830 <= 32768), whereas 81920 is sized for the Kaggle swarm's K=4. Applied identically to both arms, so it cannot bias the comparison; it does mean neither arm is byte-identical to the Kaggle configuration. THIRD DEVIATION -- explore_budget 24 vs the shipped-routed 80. Every cell ran at run_bounded_progress's explore_budget=24 default. The SCORED path passes explore_budget=None and resolves it through _route_explore_budget(strategy_route), which returns SUBMITTED_ROUTED_EXPLORE_BUDGET=24 only when uses_goal_distance_heuristic is False and SUBMITTED_GRAPH_EXPLORE_BUDGET=80 otherwise. Verified directly: all 12 candidate games AND their anonymized ids route to graph_explore with uses_goal_distance_heuristic not False, hence 80. So the measured agent induces every 24 transitions where the scored agent induces every 80 -- a ~3.3x higher induction cadence on exactly the treatment channel. It is MATCHED across arms, so it introduces no directional bias, and it is CONSERVATIVE for this artifact's verdict: the scored agent would see LESS inducer influence per run, not more, so a null here is if anything easier to obtain on the scored path.",
