+    "per_arm_engagement_required": "both arms must install >=1 induced engine",
+    "why": "A pair where NEITHER arm produced a usable plan is the same control agent twice; it contributes a tie that says nothing about the inducer. Effective discriminating support is n_pairs minus that count."
+  },
+  "falsifiability_gate_was_STRENGTHENED_after_review": "The original gate was `n_installed['31b'] + n_installed['9b'] > 0` -- an OR across arms. That is too weak: it passes whenever EITHER arm engaged, so it would have certified a run with 31b=1 / 9b=0 over 12 games as 'falsifiable' while the BASELINE arm never engaged its treatment channel at all. That failure mode is nearly as uninformative as the 2026-07-27 state the gate exists to catch, and it is not hypothetical here: the 9B reached the policy on 0 of 8 cells. The gate now requires BOTH arms to install >=1 induced engine (31b=2, 9b=1 -- it still passes, now for the right reason) and additionally reports the count of pairs with DIFFERENTIAL engagement (1 on engine acceptance, 2 on plan-found), which is the quantity that actually makes an individual pair informative about the inducer.",
+  "falsifiability_rationale": "The 2026-07-27 attempt at this question was VOIDED (verdict complete_UNFALSIFIABLE_treatment_not_applied): induction_attempts_planned == 0 on 174/174 rows because a POST-generation trust gate rejected every induced model before a plan could be installed, so the 'LLM arms' were the control agent relabelled and the delta was an arithmetic identity. This run therefore records THREE escalating witnesses per cell -- induction fired, induced engine ACCEPTED by the held-out verifier (i.e. installed as the agent's world model), and a plan found and executed. If no cell in EITHER arm had reached witness 2, this artifact would report blocked_treatment_not_applied, not a null.",
+  "field_principles": {
+    "banked_levels": "principle: a level only counts once it REPRODUCES offline; a live-recorded trajectory is exactly what the ARC Solve Reproducibility discipline says does NOT count, so the primary metric is replay-gated.",
+    "deviation_from_the_shipped_live_config": "principle: an undeclared config deviation is how a measurement silently stops describing the system it claims to describe.",
+    "inference_substrate": "principle: declares which duration floor applies, so a fabricated fast run cannot pass as live inference.",
+    "measurement_is_falsifiable": "principle: a delta between two arms that are secretly the same agent is an arithmetic identity, not a null; this gate is what separates 'the inducer does not help' from 'we never applied the treatment'.",
+    "minimum_reachable_p_at_achieved_discordance": "principle: stating the p FLOOR prevents reading an underpowered screen as a significance test.",
+    "random_seed": "principle: determinism is the precondition for a third party re-running this and getting the same pairs.",
+    "reproducibility_checksum": "principle: content-addressed hash of the per-cell rows catches silent corpus or model drift between this artifact and any replication.",
+    "solve_provenance": "principle: distinguishes an advance the LIVE agent could make on a hidden game from one an outer-loop session hand-engineered; mis-stamping it would make wasted effort look like capability."
+  },
